# The root page of a sample LDES 2.0: the first 10 000 elements of the RiverBench dataset "OpenAIRE LOD graph"
# (https://w3id.org/riverbench/datasets/openaire-lod/dev).
#
# RiverBench (https://w3id.org/riverbench) publishes benchmark datasets of RDF streams, in Jelly-RDF among others.
# Every stream element is the set of triples (in the default graph) about one scientific result in OpenAIRE. The Jelly
# file that RiverBench hosts (3.0 MB, 10 000 stream elements, stream types stax:flatTripleStream,
# stax:subjectGraphStream) is the one page of this LDES. It has no description message, so every message in the file
# is a member message: one Jelly frame is one member.
#
# How this maps to LDES (everything RiverBench says about the dataset itself is in ../catalog.ttl):
#  * membership: every message has exactly one subject of type lod:ResultEntity, with an IRI of its own: that is the
#    member identifier.
#  * ordering: RiverBench states a time of collection for each element (lod:dateofcollection), but the values are
#    xsd:string literals with different timezones, and not xsd:dateTime, so they cannot be the ldes:timestampPath.
#    There is no ldes:timestampPath: the order of the file is the order of the LDES.
#  * ldes:shape: the shape that every member conforms to (checked on all members by the generator).
#  * ldes:immutable: the Jelly file never changes, so a client that has read it does not fetch it again.
#  * the file has 10 000 messages and 10 000 distinct member identifiers, as RiverBench states
#    (rb:hasStreamElementCount). This was checked when this file was generated.
#
# Try it:  npx ldes-client https://ldes.tech/riverbench/openaire-lod/root.trig
# Generated by scripts/generate-riverbench.mjs of the ldes.tech repository; do not edit by hand.
#
@prefix ldes: <https://w3id.org/ldes#> .
@prefix lod: <http://lod.openaire.eu/vocab/> .
@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix sh: <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#> .

# The LDES: the IRI of this event stream is the root page, with a different fragment identifier
<#EventStream> a ldes:EventStream ;
    ldes:memberType lod:ResultEntity ;
    ldes:shape <#MemberShape> .

# The focus node of this shape is the member identifier
<#MemberShape> a sh:NodeShape ;
    sh:property [
        sh:path rdf:type ;
        sh:hasValue lod:ResultEntity ;
        sh:minCount 1
    ] .

# The root page itself. It has a relation to the page with all the members of this LDES.
# The elements have no timestamp to order on, so the order is that of the pages and of the members in them (implicit order):
# this is page number 0, and its members are in the order of the file.
<> ldes:relation [
    ldes:page <https://w3id.org/riverbench/datasets/openaire-lod/dev/files/jelly_10K.jelly.gz> ;
    ldes:pageNumber 0
] .

# A page can be marked immutable by the page that links to it, before it is fetched.
# This is stated about the linked page, not about the relation.
<https://w3id.org/riverbench/datasets/openaire-lod/dev/files/jelly_10K.jelly.gz> ldes:immutable true .
